# Coded by Aditya | GitHub- @adityatheog

# =============================================================================
# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# Two purposes, and the first is a security requirement rather than an
# optimisation:
#
#   Secrets must never enter the build context. Anything sent to the daemon can
#   end up in an image layer, and an image layer published to a registry is
#   public to everyone who can pull it. A .env file copied into an image is a
#   credential leak that survives every later deletion of the file, because
#   layers are immutable.
#
#   The context should stay small. Everything listed here would otherwise be
#   uploaded to the Docker daemon on every build — node_modules alone is tens of
#   thousands of files, and the host's copy is compiled against the host's libc
#   rather than the image's, so shipping it would be actively wrong.
#
# The Dockerfile also copies only four specific paths rather than using COPY . .
# That is deliberate redundancy: if this file were misconfigured, an enumerated
# copy still cannot pull in a local .env.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — the reason this file exists
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every variant, because .env.production and .env.local are just as sensitive.
.env
.env.*
# The template carries no values and documents every variable, but it is not
# needed at runtime either.
.env.example

*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json
service-account*.json


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded for correctness, not just size. better-sqlite3 compiles a native addon
# against the host's Node version and libc; copying the host's node_modules into a
# Debian-based image produces an addon that fails at require time. The build stage
# compiles its own.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.npm
.yarn
.pnp
.pnp.js
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The database holds real user records and the Discord-to-panel mapping. Baking a
# development copy into an image would publish those records and give every
# container the same stale starting state.
data
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db

# The liveness file. A stale copy in the image would make the health check report
# healthy for the first minute before the process had written anything.
heartbeat

logs
*.log


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and CI
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .git can be larger than the entire source tree, and its history may contain
# credentials that were committed and later removed — history keeps them.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests and tooling
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The suite runs in CI and locally, never inside the production image. Excluding
# it keeps the runtime image to the code that actually serves commands.
tests
coverage
.nyc_output


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Useful in the repository, dead weight in a container.
docs
*.md
LICENSE


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Container and deployment definitions
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The image does not need the files that describe how to build or deploy it, and
# a compose override could reference host paths that do not exist inside it.
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
deploy


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and packaging output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist
build
out
*.tgz
*.zip
*.tar.gz


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.eslintcache
.editorconfig

.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Process managers and local overrides
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pm2
ecosystem.config.cjs
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock
config.local.json
